{"builder":"Make one pull request for https://github.com/o/strutil/issues/7 that meets every one of these acceptance lines:\n- index.js exports padLeft(s, width, fill), which pads s on the left with fill (a space when fill is not given) to width characters\n- padLeft returns s unchanged when s is already width characters or longer\n- README.md has a section for every function index.js exports\n- npm test passes\n\nSteps:\n1. Read index.js, README.md, package.json and test/strutil.test.js. The package is an ES module (\"type\": \"module\"); index.js currently exports capitalize, slugify and truncate. `npm test` runs `node --test`.\n2. In index.js add and export `padLeft(s, width, fill = ' ')` with a short doc comment in the style of the existing functions. It returns `s` unchanged when `s.length >= width`; otherwise it adds `fill` on the left until the result is exactly `width` characters (e.g. padLeft('42', 5, '0') === '00042', padLeft('ab', 4) === '  ab'). `s.padStart(width, fill)` meets this for a one-character fill. Do not change the existing functions.\n3. In README.md make sure there is a section for EVERY function index.js exports, not only the new one. Note that README.md today has sections for capitalize and truncate but NONE for slugify, so add a `## slugify(s)` section (describe it: lower case, runs of non-alphanumerics become single dashes, leading/trailing dashes removed) as well as a `## padLeft(s, width, fill)` section (pads on the left with fill, default a space, to width characters; returns s unchanged when already width or longer; mention the 42 -> 00042 example). Use the same `## name(args)` heading style as the existing sections and keep them before the `## Tests` section.\n4. In test/strutil.test.js import padLeft and add tests: padLeft('42', 5, '0') === '00042'; padLeft('ab', 4) === '  ab' (default space); padLeft('abcde', 5, '0') === 'abcde' and padLeft('abcdef', 3) === 'abcdef' (unchanged when already width or longer).\n5. Run `npm test` and confirm it exits 0 with all tests passing. Also check that every name in `node -e \"import('./index.js').then(m=>console.log(Object.keys(m)))\"` has a matching heading in README.md.\n6. Commit and open the pull request referencing issue #7.","verifier":"Check out the pull request head and run every check below from the repository root. There is one check per acceptance line of https://github.com/o/strutil/issues/7, in the same order. Report PASS or FAIL for each with the command output that decided it.\n\nCheck 1 — \"index.js exports padLeft(s, width, fill), which pads s on the left with fill (a space when fill is not given) to width characters\"\nRun: node --input-type=module -e \"import * as m from './index.js'; console.log(typeof m.padLeft); console.log(JSON.stringify([m.padLeft('42',5,'0'), m.padLeft('ab',4), m.padLeft('7',3,'*'), m.padLeft('',2,'x')]))\"\nPASS: first line is `function` and the array is [\"00042\",\"  ab\",\"**7\",\"xx\"] (padding added on the left with the given fill, a space when fill is omitted, result exactly width characters long).\nFAIL: padLeft is not exported, throws, pads on the right, uses a different default than a space, or any result is not width characters long.\n\nCheck 2 — \"padLeft returns s unchanged when s is already width characters or longer\"\nRun: node --input-type=module -e \"import {padLeft} from './index.js'; console.log(JSON.stringify([padLeft('abcde',5,'0'), padLeft('abcdef',3), padLeft('abcdef',3,'0')]))\"\nPASS: output is [\"abcde\",\"abcdef\",\"abcdef\"].\nFAIL: any value differs from its input s (padded, truncated or otherwise changed), or the call throws.\n\nCheck 3 — \"README.md has a section for every function index.js exports\"\nRun: node --input-type=module -e \"import * as m from './index.js'; console.log(Object.keys(m).filter(k=>typeof m[k]==='function').join(' '))\" to list exported functions, then read README.md (e.g. `grep -n '^#' README.md`) and look for a section for each listed name.\nPASS: every exported function (expected at least capitalize, slugify, truncate, padLeft) has its own section in README.md, i.e. a heading that names that function, with text describing it.\nFAIL: any exported function has no section in README.md. Note: before this change README.md had no slugify section, so check slugify specifically.\n\nCheck 4 — \"npm test passes\"\nRun: npm test\nPASS: the test run reports all tests passing (no failures).\nFAIL: any test fails or the run errors.\n\nAdvisory (not pass/fail conditions):\n- Expect `npm test` to exit with status 0 and to include tests for padLeft (default fill and the unchanged case).\n- Existing functions capitalize, slugify and truncate should behave as before.\n- README section headings would ideally follow the existing `## name(args)` style and appear before `## Tests`."}